  "text": "Planning Document: docs/dcps/INNERWEST/Marrickville/Marrickville DCP 2011 - 9 45 McGill Street Precinct 45.pdf\n\nClause 9.45.2 - environmental_protection (environmental_protection): This precinct has been identified as having high biodiversity values. It is essential that development within the precinct  conside rs the potential  impacts to biodiversity including native fauna (including Threatened S pecies and Endangered P opulations); native vegetation (including Endangered E cological C ommunities); and habitat elem ents (including  their condition , structure, function, connectivity a nd disturbance).\n\nClause 9.45.3 - zoning (land_use_zoning): As it is redeveloped, the precinct will fit appropriately into the heart of Lewisham as  a village -type locality accommodating mixed use development of high to medium densities and scales.\n\nClause 9.45.3 - zoning (land_use_zoning): The precinct will  accomm odate some minor service retail, commercial offices and showrooms as well as studio, cafe and restaurant spaces .\n\n",
